Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:54:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: give every page chrome.app, chrome.csi and
 chrome.loadTimes

Chrome's renderer gives every page window.chrome.app, chrome.csi and
chrome.loadTimes, and QtWebEngine gave none of them. Google's sign-in
turns away a Chrome-like browser without chrome.app ("This browser or
app may not be secure", rrk=46). An application can define a stand-in
with a script, but a page tells it from Chrome's by reading a
function's source, which is plain JavaScript where Chrome's reads
[native code].

Define them as Chrome does:

- chrome.app comes from the extension bindings system, which offers the
  "app" namespace to every web page (kWebAvailableFeatures). Copy
  Chrome's app.json schema into QtWebEngine's uncompiled schemas, give
  it Chrome's feature in _webengine_api_features.json, less the
  blocklist of Google's own extensions, and register
  Chrome's AppHooksDelegate in the renderer API provider. The delegate
  answers every function in the renderer.
- installState() asks the browser, and ExtensionFrameHost answered with
  an empty string. QtWebEngine installs no hosted app, so it now
  answers "not_installed", as Chrome does for such a page.
- chrome.csi and chrome.loadTimes are Chrome's v8 extension
  (chrome/renderer/loadtimes_extension_bindings.cc), registered when the
  render thread starts, as ChromeContentRendererClient does.

windowChromeAnswersAsChromeDoes reads the three in the main world and
in a same-origin, an about:blank and a srcdoc frame, and compares them
with Chromium 154's answers for a page that is not an installed app: the members of chrome.app, getDetails()
reading [native code], csi() and loadTimes() returning their fields,
and installState() calling back with "not_installed".

See villekivela/omaweb#766.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
